WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.370
When your phone runs low, you plug
it in, and it charges back up.

2
00:00:04.420 --> 00:00:08.090
When a standard AA battery
goes flat, it's finished.

3
00:00:08.140 --> 00:00:09.650
Off to be recycled.

4
00:00:09.700 --> 00:00:13.190
Both turn chemical energy
into electrical energy.

5
00:00:13.240 --> 00:00:16.170
So why can one be recharged,
and not the other?

6
00:00:16.220 --> 00:00:20.570
Why can you recharge a phone battery,
but not a standard AA battery?

7
00:00:20.620 --> 00:00:24.530
In this mission, you'll build a
voltaic cell from zinc and copper,

8
00:00:24.580 --> 00:00:28.930
and track the electrons in the wire
and the ions in the salt bridge.

9
00:00:28.980 --> 00:00:32.670
You'll compare primary cells,
secondary cells and fuel cells,

10
00:00:32.720 --> 00:00:35.130
and weigh up their trade-offs.

11
00:00:35.180 --> 00:00:40.830
Your mission: explain why a phone battery
can be recharged, but an AA battery can't.
